  "title": "epan: Remove a too-late NULL check",
  "description": "proto_register_field_common checks if proto is NULL, but proto has\nalready been deferenced in proto_register_field_array (and was\nsimilarly dereferenced in the now removed NEW_PROTO_TREE_API).\n\nApparently it hasn't been a problem, but if we want to check if\nproto is NULL, we should do it once at the top of proto_register_field_array\nand not once each iteration of a potentially large loop.\n\nProfiling and examination of generated assembly shows that many\ncompilers do not remove this null check.",
